# =============================================================================
# VST-Development .gitignore
# Comprehensive patterns to prevent artifact accumulation
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# Claude Configuration
# =============================================================================
.claude/system-config.json

# =============================================================================
# Python Bytecode
# =============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# =============================================================================
# Ouaricon module-system build artifacts
# =============================================================================
# OuariconModules.cmake auto-copies module JS into Source/ui/public/modules/
# at configure time as a fallback for plugins that consume modules through
# that path. Plugins like O-MicrotonalSampler instead serve module JS via
# the WebView resource provider, making this directory a build-time leftover
# that should not be committed.
plugins/*/Source/ui/public/modules/

# =============================================================================
# Backup Directories
# =============================================================================
# Prevent large backup folders from being committed.
# Backups are local-only safety nets for the /improve workflow; release
# history is preserved via git tags (e.g. v1.6.0-O-MicrotonalSampler), so
# committing parallel backup snapshots would just bloat history with
# duplicates of source already in git.
backups/

# =============================================================================
# Render-Harness / Test-Capture Scratch Output
# =============================================================================
# Per-plugin render-harness produces JSON status files and binary WAV
# captures alongside the source tree. The JSON files at repo root are
# clearly misplaced (harness was run from the wrong cwd) and ignored
# everywhere; the binary WAV evidence lives in .planning/evidence/ and is
# regenerable from source — no value committing the binary captures.
e1-max-sustain.json
*-pre-extraction-canonical.json
plugins/*/.planning/evidence/**/*.wav
#
# O-Bowed's canonical golden render is a special case. The `.sha256` sibling
# already in that directory IS the tracked audit trail — it is what any future
# harness run is checked against. The binary itself is kept on disk purely as a
# local byte-exact reference and is deliberately not committed.
#
# Why this one is ignored when O-Contrabass tracks its own golden renders:
# section 4.2 of PUBLIC-RELEASE-READINESS.md identifies the tracked audio
# goldens as the single largest contributor to repository size, and step 14
# exists to reclaim exactly that. Adding another multi-megabyte binary to a
# now-public repo would work against that standing direction, and O-Bowed's
# golden directory was authored sha256-only from the start — this preserves the
# author's original choice rather than quietly reversing it.
#
# Why this names one exact path and not a directory wildcard: O-Contrabass
# legitimately tracks nineteen golden renders in its own golden directory, so a
# broader rule would silently stop future intentional goldens from being
# tracked. Same reasoning as the installer block at the end of this file —
# match the artifact, never broaden to the containing directory.
plugins/O-Bowed/tests/render-harness/golden/canonical-preset.wav

